  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, thanks for reporting this. I checked your mailbox and there is no quarantined message that could be the meeting invite, and your account is active with no sign-in problems. To narrow it down, could you reply with: (1) who organized the Q4 planning meeting, (2) whether you have an assistant or delegate who manages your calendar, and (3) whether the meeting shows up when you open your calendar in Outlook on the web (outlook.office.com) as well as in the desktop app. Once we have that, we can fix it or ask the organizer to resend the invite.",
  "internal_note": "Sofia Rossi (user_id 7, Marketing Coordinator, device BL-LT-0107). Account active, not locked, no failed logins, sign-in not blocked. Spam quarantine for her mailbox is empty, so the invite was not held. Not yet checked: whether a delegate receives her calendar invites (lookup tool does not expose delegate settings), and OWA vs desktop comparison (user has not reported). Asked user for organizer name, delegate info, and OWA vs desktop result. If the organizer is an internal user and invites from them never arrive, escalate per KB-012 (possible mail rule or transport issue). No action queued.",
